<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Misima</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Misima is an island of the Louisiade Archipelago in Milne Bay Province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papua-new-guinea">Papua New Guinea</a>. Gold was found there in the 1880s, attracting prospectors in the early days of British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-guinea">New Guinea</a>, and a large modern gold mine operated on the island from 1989 to 2004.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/misima.jpg" alt="Misima" width="320" height="112" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Givet · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Misima_Island.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
